From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 20:22:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] msm8996-common: ims: ImsBridge, the compat ImsService over
 LG's Ims4

Ims4 registers with the network but nothing in the A17 telephony stack sees
it: ImsResolver binds an ImsService, and LG's is a ServiceManager entry
("ims") speaking the com.android.ims API Android 9 deleted. ImsBridge
implements the compat MMTelFeature over it, so no framework patch is needed.

Generated from forge/templates/ims-bridge (new-ims-bridge.sh --legacy-pkg
com.lge.imslegacy --oem-app Ims4 --device vs995 --restrict-cause); the legacy
com.lge.imslegacy AIDL under bridge/aidl is emitted by build-ims4.sh step 2.7
from the same stock framework the app was reworked against, and checked
against the stock $Stub transaction tables with aidl-tx-diff.py -- LG's
IImsService is the 7.0 shape (15 transactions), one method short of 7.1's.

Two shape differences from a 7.1 bridge, both found by reading Ims4's smali:
LG's open() takes a single registration listener and setRegistrationListener
replaces it, so the bridge hands down ONE multicast adapter and replays the
cached state to listeners the framework adds later; and the feature bitmap is
only emitted on a UC reg-state change, so a bridge that opens after
registration completed must rebuild it from isConnected(id, NORMAL,
VOICE/VT) or every call goes CS.

build-ims4.sh step 3.5 replaces the build-time parcelable stubs with the
stock framework's real smali (ImsCallProfile: 51 fields, not 1) -- they live
in boot-framework's classes2.dex, which is why a single-entry deodex missed
them and REGISTER worked while a call would have arrived with no number.

Wiring: ImsBridge and the telephony.ims feature xml (without it PhoneGlobals
never constructs an ImsResolver), config_ims_mmtel_package, and
ro.telephony.block_binder_thread_on_incoming_calls=false.
